Objective-C class, protocol and superclass references in __DATA_CONST from iOS and tvOS 17.4, macOS 14.4, watchOS 10.4
and visionOS 1.1 (and for arm64 watchOS), and from iOS and tvOS 18, macOS 15, watchOS 11 and visionOS 2 class
references loaded through the GOT instead of __objc_classrefs: a load of a class reference (arm64 adrp and ldr, x86_64
movq) becomes a GOT load of the class, bound for a class of a dylib and relaxed to computing its address for a class
of the image, and the class references only loaded that way are not written, as Xcode 27.0's ld links them (docs/formats/
build.md "Objective-C references in the linked image"; swiftfin's image had them in __DATA).
